    <origin>Session 26 verified defect C6 (notes/session26-uac-defects-and-synopsis.md § C6). Known since investigation gap G-10 (notes/investigation/05-three-plane-completeness.md:36, :127) but never promoted to the register, spec, a task or an issue. Owner round 2 (2026-09-30): no scope cuts, nothing deferred.</origin>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>The external module read seam lets any CIAM or workforce caller write their own FetchXML (POST /api/v1/external/api/dataverse/fetch) or $select (GET /record), executes it app-only, and returns every column it asked for. Row scope is enforced; column scope is not. Add a per-module column allow-list and enforce it before execution and again on the result, so SPE pointers and internal or field-secured columns can no longer be projected by an external caller.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE BFF security engineer — the external module-host read seam (FR-22 / ADR-028 A3) and FetchXML handling. You are narrowing what a shipped external SPA can read; treat every column you drop as a possible broken grid and prove it is not.</role>

  <goal>Every ExternalModuleDescriptor declares the exact columns an external caller may read from its entity. /fetch refuses (400, stable error code) any FetchXML that uses all-attributes or references a non-allow-listed attribute anywhere (attribute, condition, order, aggregate/alias); /record refuses or drops non-allow-listed $select fields; and both responses strip any non-allow-listed key (including its @formattedValues entry) as defence in depth. The six outside-counsel grids still render with their live grid configurations.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>🔴 LIVE, verified 2026-09-30 against source.

THE ROUTE. `Api/ExternalAccess/ExternalModuleDataEndpoints.cs:84` maps POST /fetch and `:95` maps GET /record/{entity}/{id}; the group is mounted unconditionally under /api/v1/external (EndpointMappingExtensions.cs:439) and reached by BOTH planes (CallerPrincipalAuthorizationFilter). The file header at `:26-27` promises "no Graph pointer ever reaches the client" — the code does not keep that promise.

WHAT THE GUARD CHECKS TODAY. `EvaluateFetchXmlGuard` (`:502-548`) refuses (1) any entity other than the module's own (`:526-530`) and (2) any link-entity at any depth (`:545-547`, task 011 / FR-10). It never looks at `attribute`, `all-attributes`, `condition attribute=`, `order attribute=` or aliases.

WHAT SCOPING CHECKS TODAY. `Tier2ScopeFilterInjector.Inject` (`Api/ExternalAccess/Tier2ScopeFilterInjector.cs:84`) appends a row filter, and `ExternalModuleDescriptor.ScopeRows` (`Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/ExternalModuleRegistry.cs:153-187`) drops out-of-scope ROWS. Nothing filters COLUMNS.

WHAT EXECUTES. `FetchService.ExecuteAsync` (`Services/Dataverse/FetchService.cs:95-96`) runs the FetchXML through the app-only ServiceClient — which bypasses field-level security — and `ProjectEntity` (`:141-169`) copies EVERY returned attribute plus `@formattedValues` to the response. ⚠️ FetchService is SHARED with the internal /api/dataverse surface: do NOT put the external allow-list inside FetchService.

WHAT LEAKS. A granted contact can request `sprk_graphdriveid`, `sprk_graphitemid`, `sprk_filepath` (the Graph webUrl) on every in-scope `sprk_document` — exactly the pointers the curated document read deliberately omits (`Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/ExternalDataService.cs:211`) and the upload path writes (`:252-260`). Any other internal or FLS-secured column on sprk_document / sprk_invoice / the three roots is equally readable.

/record. `GetScopedRecordAsync` (`ExternalModuleDataEndpoints.cs:243-301`) passes `$select` straight through `ParseSelect` (`:632-645`) to `RecordService.GetRecordAsync` (`Services/Dataverse/RecordService.cs:57-74`). With no $select it projects only primary id + primary name (`:113-154`), which is safe; with a $select it projects anything. Child single-record reads fail the Tier-2 gate (`ExternalModuleRegistry.cs:125-144`), so /record exposes arbitrary columns of granted ROOT records (e.g. `sprk_project.sprk_containerid`) and of the grid-configuration records.

THE REGISTERED MODULES (all in `Infrastructure/DI/ExternalAccessModule.cs`): collaboration/sprk_project `:224-230`, documents/sprk_document `:244-254`, invoices/sprk_invoice `:259-268`, work-assignments/sprk_workassignment `:274-280`, matters/sprk_matter `:286-292`, service-requests/sprk_servicerequest `:299-308`, grid-configuration/sprk_gridconfiguration `:318-324`. ⚠️ The type is `ExternalModuleDescriptor`, not "ExternalModuleDefinition" as the session-26 fix direction wrote.

WHERE THE LEGITIMATE COLUMN LIST COMES FROM. The external SPA's grids (`src/client/external-spa/src/widgets/*`, via `gridDataverseClient.ts` and the shared `DataGrid`) do not carry their FetchXML in the repo: each grid loads a `sprk_gridconfiguration` record (the six ids at `ExternalAccessModule.cs:31-39`; its `sprk_fetchxml` / `sprk_layoutxml` / `sprk_configjson` columns) and may also load saved queries through the passthrough `/savedquery` routes. The allow-list must therefore be derived from those LIVE records plus each module's scope-dimension attributes (the injector filters on them and `ScopeRows` needs them projected, `ExternalModuleRegistry.cs:178`). The grid-configuration module's OWN allow-list comes from the columns the shared client selects when it reads a configuration record through /record (`src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/services/ConfigurationService.ts:68`, `:149`; `ViewService.ts:314`). An allow-list written from memory will blank a grid.

NEW MODULES. Task 056 (pending) registers sprk_todo / sprk_event / sprk_communication as child modules. Whichever of 134 and 056 lands second must give those descriptors allow-lists; after this task, `Register` refuses a descriptor without one, so 056 cannot silently register an all-columns module.</background>
