  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-003">Scope: every refusal path added by this task. Fail CLOSED: a module with no declared allow-list refuses every /fetch and every /record $select for that module (registration must not silently default to "all columns"); an unparseable FetchXML refuses; an unmodelled verdict refuses — mirror the existing `default:` arm of `RejectFetchXml` (`ExternalModuleDataEndpoints.cs:603-613`).</constraint>
    <constraint source="C6 fix direction">Scope: /fetch. REJECT, do not silently rewrite, a FetchXML that uses `all-attributes` or names a non-allow-listed attribute in ANY position: `attribute name=`, `attribute alias=` (an alias must not smuggle a column under another key), `condition attribute=` (a filter on a hidden column is a value oracle), `order attribute=`, and aggregate/groupby attributes. The response is 400 ProblemDetails with a new stable errorCode, distinct from `DV_FETCHXML_ENTITY_MISMATCH` and `DV_FETCHXML_LINK_ENTITY_NOT_PERMITTED`. Evaluate it inside the SAME single authority, `EvaluateFetchXmlGuard`, as a third ordered signal after entity identity and link-entity — no second guard method.</constraint>
    <constraint source="C6 fix direction">Scope: /record. A `$select` naming any non-allow-listed column is refused with 400 and the same errorCode family (do not silently drop — a silently narrowed read is indistinguishable from a null value). The no-$select default projection (primary id + primary name) must itself be allow-listed for every module.</constraint>
    <constraint source="C6 fix direction">Scope: defence in depth, both routes. After execution AND after `ScopeRows` (so row scoping still sees its scope attributes), strip every key not on the module allow-list from each returned row, including the matching entry inside `@formattedValues`; keep the synthetic `@logicalName` key that `ScopeRows` requires (`ExternalModuleRegistry.cs:195-204`). Aliased keys are not allow-listed columns and are stripped. This runs in the external endpoint, NOT in the shared FetchService or RecordService.</constraint>
    <constraint source="broker-only / ADR-028 A1-A3">Scope: the allow-lists. `sprk_graphdriveid`, `sprk_graphitemid`, `sprk_filepath`, and any container / drive / item / webUrl pointer column (`sprk_containerid`, `sprk_specontainerid` and equivalents on the roots) MUST NOT appear on any external module's allow-list. File access stays on the document-id-keyed routes.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §11">Scope: the allow-list's home. Extend the existing `ExternalModuleDescriptor` (one new property) and validate it in `ExternalModuleRegistry.Register` (`:266-292`) — no new registry, no new service, no new filter, no configuration file.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner 2026-09-10 / spec">Scope: verification. No Dataverse test runs in CI. The live grid check is a MANUAL gate using the existing non-admin test users and an existing CIAM test contact in the correct BU. Do NOT propose relocating any user.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Scope: tests. Authorization-behaviour tests go to the KEEP path `tests/integration/auth/UnifiedAccessControl/`; no `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`, no DI-registration tests, no constructor null-check tests.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §10">Scope: this task's PR. State the placement decision (in BFF, extending the existing seam) citing `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md`; measure publish size against a FRESH master worktree and a fresh branch worktree, both from SHORT paths, same zip tool (Compress-Archive), equal file counts on both sides; report both sizes and the delta; ceiling 60 MB; no new HIGH CVE (`dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive`).</constraint>
  </constraints>

