  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0">Re-verify every anchor above against current source; this project has repeated premise rot. Confirm FetchService/RecordService are shared with the internal /api/dataverse routes before deciding where stripping lives.</step>
    <step order="1">Derive each module's allow-list from LIVE data: read the six `sprk_gridconfiguration` records (`ExternalAccessModule.cs:31-39`) and any saved query or saved view the external grids load, list every attribute they reference (attribute, condition, order, alias, aggregate positions), add each module's scope-dimension attributes and the /record default projection, derive the grid-configuration module's list from the shared client's /record `$select` (ConfigurationService.ts, ViewService.ts), and record the derivation (record id or source file → columns) in the task notes. Remove pointer columns per the broker-only constraint; if a live grid references one, or uses an alias or aggregate, fire the escalation.</step>
    <step order="2">Add the allow-list property to `ExternalModuleDescriptor`, validate it at `Register` (non-empty; contains every scope-dimension attribute; contains the /record default columns; contains no pointer column), and declare it on every registration present at execution time (seven today; ten if task 056 has landed).</step>
    <step order="3">Add the column signal to `EvaluateFetchXmlGuard` and its `RejectFetchXml` arm; enforce the /record `$select` rule; add post-execution key stripping on both routes.</step>
    <step order="4">Fix the file-header promise at `ExternalModuleDataEndpoints.cs:26-27` so it describes the mechanism that now keeps it.</step>
    <step order="5">Tests per the closed set below, with perturbations; build, full unit suite, ArchTests, publish size.</step>
    <step order="6">MANUAL live gate against dev (see acceptance). Record the result in `projects/unified-access-control-r2/notes/task-134-external-module-column-allow-list.md`.</step>
    <step order="7">Update TASK-INDEX.md (status token `✅ [done]`) and this POML's status; run `pwsh scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1`.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>A live grid configuration or saved query used by an external widget legitimately projects a pointer column (sprk_graphdriveid / sprk_graphitemid / sprk_filepath / a container id). STOP — that is a product decision about what the grid shows, not an allow-list detail. Report the record, the column and the widget.</trigger>
    <trigger>The column list a widget needs cannot be derived because a grid configuration or saved query is unreadable or missing in dev. STOP rather than guessing a list; a guessed list either leaks or blanks a grid.</trigger>
    <trigger>An internal (non-external) consumer turns out to reach FetchService or RecordService through the external route group. STOP; the fix must not change the internal /api/dataverse surface.</trigger>
    <trigger>A live grid configuration or saved query used by an external widget projects an ALIASED or AGGREGATE attribute. STOP — the reject-alias rule and the post-execution strip would blank that column. Report the record and the expression; RECOMMENDATION: rewrite the grid's FetchXML to the plain attribute (the alias carries no security meaning) rather than allow-listing alias keys.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>`ExternalModuleDescriptor` (`Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/ExternalModuleRegistry.cs:72-238`) already carries each module's ROW scope (`ScopeDimensions`, `RecordIdAttribute`); `EvaluateFetchXmlGuard` (`ExternalModuleDataEndpoints.cs:502`) is the single FetchXML authority. Grep for a column allow-list on this seam (`AllowedColumns|AllowList|allowedAttributes` under Api/ExternalAccess and Infrastructure/ExternalAccess) finds none.</existing>
    <extension>Yes — this task EXTENDS both: one new property on the existing descriptor and one new ordered signal inside the existing guard. No new type, service, filter or route.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>A CIAM contact granted on one project POSTs a FetchXML selecting sprk_graphdriveid, sprk_graphitemid and sprk_filepath on sprk_document and receives the SPE drive id, item id and Graph webUrl of every document on that project (app-only, FLS bypassed), contradicting the broker-only invariant the route's own header states.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

